# Case bb of the wedge lemma: the polynomial inequality

`Gbb C S cp sp cq sq ap aq` is `sqrt 2 * (rest - (2 + 4 sqrt 2 / 3) * coefL)` for the case-bb bound of
`s19/tools/wedge_cases.c` (`pa = qa = 0`), written in `C = cos a13`, `S = sin a13`,
`cp, sp = cos, sin (a14 - a13)`, `cq, sq = cos, sin (a11 - a13)`, with `ap = |sp|`, `aq = |sq|`.
The four theorems below prove `Gbb >= 0` in each sign orthant of `(sp, sq)` on a box that contains the
capture range. Each proof is an exact Handelman-type identity (products of the box constraints with
nonnegative rational weights, plus polynomial multiples of the three Pythagorean identities), found by
LP in `s19/tools` style scratch code and checked here by `ring` (via `linear_combination`).
